Description: Slide between workspaces, and a pill of dots as their OSD
 Switching workspaces in Labwc is a cut: the windows of one workspace vanish
 and those of the next appear. On macOS the old space slides out to one side
 while the new one comes in from the other, so the user sees where they went.
 This patch adds that, off by default, and a lighter OSD to go with it.
 .
 <desktops slideTime="500">: before a switch every output that shows the
 group is rendered into a buffer of its own (wlr_scene_output_build_state
 with a private swapchain), without the top and overlay layers, menus, OSDs
 and software cursors; after the switch it is rendered again. Two scene
 buffers above the windows and below the top layer then show the part of
 each snapshot that is on screen, cropped with source boxes, so a panel stays
 put and nothing spills onto a neighbouring output. The output frame handler
 advances them on cubic-bezier(0.25, 1, 0.5, 1) until slideTime has passed.
 A switch during a slide ends it where it was going. Rotated outputs, a locked
 session and slideTime="0" switch at once. Each snapshot is followed by full
 damage, since the real output has not seen that render.
 .
 <desktops popupStyle="dots">: the workspace OSD becomes a pill near the
 bottom of the output, one dot per workspace with the current one drawn
 long, and its name, in the OSD theme colours with the window switcher's
 active colour as accent. It stays for popupTime whether or not modifiers
 are held, since a quick key press would otherwise hide it before the slide
 ends.
 .
 Known limits: windows are frozen during a slide (a video pauses for half a
 second); omnipresent windows slide out and back in.
Author: The Dodobian authors
Origin: vendor, https://github.com/dodobian/dodobian/tree/main/labwc
Forwarded: no
---
