 	Changing it takes effect after a restart.
 
+*<desktops slideTime="">*
+	Slide from one workspace to the next, in milliseconds, as on macOS:
+	the old workspace leaves the output to one side while the new one
+	comes in from the other, on a curve that starts fast and settles
+	slowly. Layer-shell surfaces of the top and overlay layers, such as a
+	panel, stay where they are. Each output slides on its own and nothing
+	spills onto a neighbouring output. Rotated outputs switch at once.
+	Default is 0: no slide.
+
+*<desktops popupStyle="">* [classic|dots]
+	The look of the workspace switcher OSD. "dots" draws a pill near the
+	bottom of the output: one dot per workspace, the current one long, and
+	its name. It stays for popupTime whether or not modifiers are held.
+	Default is classic.
+
 ## THEME
 
 *<theme><name>*
